> jails/instances/lab-mail: Deliver posts to INBOX and sync it" [2]:
>
> - mbsyncrc has "Patterns INBOX Archive lists", and mbsync syncs no
>   other folder. I took ARCHIVE to mean the folder Archive, Fastmail's
>   archive folder, since IMAP folder names are case-sensitive.

Yes that's correct

A couple things... I am getting rid of the lists folder. As discussed in
another thread, the folders are now:

- INBOX
- Archive
- Later
- Next
- quarantine

Additionally, I want lab-mail to sync all folders with fastmail. It's
only the mailing list clients that limit to those folders.

Some process-mail changes as well:

- only process messages tagged with inbox. This is how I can archive
  messages and not have them be processed.
- do not act on any messages other than from approved senders. If a
  message from a non-approved sender makes it through, move it to
  quarantine folder.
